<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  No hardened-runtime exceptions are needed, so none are granted:
  - JIT / unsigned executable memory: mpv scripts (and so LuaJIT) are turned off
    (load-scripts=no), and neither Qt Widgets nor FFmpeg generates machine code.
  - Library validation stays on: every bundled dylib, framework and plugin is signed
    with the same identity in the workflow, so only our own code can be loaded.
  If the signed app fails to load a library with "different Team IDs" or "code
  signature invalid", sign that file in the workflow rather than adding an exception.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
